{
  "formatVersion": 1,
  "title": "Plan values: the one definition of type, presence, range and allowed text (S5AA R43)",
  "about": "S5AA R43 (Claude's R42F audit, SA42F-05 and SA42F-06; the owner 2026-09-30: repair all 34). R42 typed two Social Security fields; R42F found the same defect in at least 25 more fields that neither layer typed or ranged and that ran silently coerced (a conversion amount of \"abc\" converted $0; an LTC probability of -10 turned care into income), six text fields neither layer checked, and ten plans the validator refused that the engine ran. Both the engine's input gate (src/engine.js) and the validator (src/scenario-validator.js) read THIS FILE, as both read src/boolean-flag-contract.json: a second hand-written list is the defect shape. A scalar entry names a dotted path; a list entry names a list and its records' fields. A number must be a finite JSON number when present (null is present); `required` makes absence an error too, and `requiredWhen` names a flag that makes it required while true. `min`/`max` bound it (`minExclusive` makes the minimum a strict bound). An `enum` value must be one of `values` when present. The engine refuses a violation (SCENARIO_NONNUMBER_PLAN_VALUE for a type or a missing value, SCENARIO_PLAN_VALUE_OUT_OF_RANGE, SCENARIO_UNKNOWN_PLAN_VALUE for text) and the validator reports it as an ERROR (WRONG_TYPE, MISSING_FIELD, OUT_OF_RANGE, INVALID_ENUM). Fields the engine already refuses under other codes keep those codes; this file adds what neither layer held.",
